cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize this software or reference these techniques in academic research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "Scientific ML on Zero Budget: Training Real Models with Free Colab/Kaggle GPUs"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/samudragupto/scientific-ml-zero-budget"
url: "https://github.com/samudragupto/scientific-ml-zero-budget"
abstract: >-
  A production-ready open-source research and educational toolkit demonstrating how to train real
  scientific machine learning models within the memory, compute, and runtime constraints of free
  cloud GPU environments (Google Colab, Kaggle). Employs automatic mixed precision, multi-step
  gradient accumulation, resilient atomic checkpointing with complete RNG state preservation,
  memory-mapped zero-RAM data streaming, and lightweight depthwise-separable architectures.
